1 | web-frontend | Wire /account/trips to real data and delete the fabrication, per docs/prd/pages/21-account-trips.md sections 6.5 and 7, which were ratified by a co-founder on 2026-08-12 under issue 2592. READ THAT SPEC FIRST and implement to it rather than inventing anything. THE DEFECT, from the audit in issue 2659: apps/web/app/account/trips/page.tsx line 104 reads const trips = RA_TRIPS, with no fetch and no flag, so every signed-in user sees the same six invented trips under the heading Booked trips, Confirmed reservations, flights, stays, dinners, all held. One of them is Tokyo, slowly with status booked and price 4280. A Friends-and-Family traveller who has genuinely booked cannot tell which card is theirs. That is the worst finding in the audit and it is a trust problem, not a cosmetic one. THREE SITES, all named by the spec. One, apps/web/app/account/trips/page.tsx: replace the fixture read with the real sources the spec names, listBookings for the booked status and listResultSessions for draft and idea. Two, the RA_TRIPS constant in apps/web/lib/atlas-v2-fixtures.ts: delete it, and check for any other importer before you do rather than assuming this page is the only one. Three, apps/web/app/account/trips/page.test.tsx: it currently pins the fixture length and the per-status counts as required UI, which means the test actively re-mandates the fabrication on every run. Rewrite it against the real data path. Do not simply delete it; a page that fetches bookings deserves tests for the loading, empty and error states. THE SPEC ALSO SETTLES THE OBVIOUS OBJECTION, so do not re-open it: a section 15 Coming-soon treatment is WRONG here because both endpoints are already live and already serve other surfaces. The store exists; this grid was simply never wired to it. Implement the loading, empty and error triad that section 6.5 ratifies, and use its empty copy exactly, which is Nothing here yet. Do not invent copy; if you need a string the spec does not contain, add it to the spec marked PROPOSED pending co-founder sign-off and say so in the PR body. VERIFY: typecheck, lint, unit tests and a production build, with real exit codes captured directly and never read after a pipe. Add coverage proving an account with zero bookings renders the empty state rather than six trips, and prove that test fails on origin/main. Check whether any visual baseline covers this page and report rather than refreshing it blindly. Open a PR referencing issue 2659 and issue 2592 with Refs, no closing keyword, since 2659 carries two other items that stay open. Do not merge. | fix/2659-a1-real-trips

2 | frontend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the wave 1 change on branch fix/2659-a1-real-trips. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels, no test writing. Permitted writes are a /tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check at report; if it moved, report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: can any signed-in user still be shown a trip that is not theirs. Verify by reading the data path end to end, not by trusting the diff: confirm RA_TRIPS is gone from the tree rather than merely unreferenced, confirm no other module still imports it, and confirm the booked status is sourced from listBookings rather than from anything client-side or seeded. SECOND: verify the rewritten page test genuinely exercises the real data path and no longer pins fixture counts, and that the zero-bookings empty-state test actually fails on origin/main, reproducing that yourself in a throwaway worktree rather than accepting the claim. THIRD: check the loading, empty and error states match docs/prd/pages/21-account-trips.md section 6.5, that the empty copy is exactly Nothing here yet, and that no string was invented outside the spec without a PROPOSED marker. FOURTH: confirm the change did not quietly widen scope into audit items A2 or A3, which are the profile counters and the activities picker, both of which need product decisions and are deliberately out of scope. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC 2659 A1, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE plus per-finding severity and file:line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | fix/2659-a1-real-trips
